{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Do you know Laban the son of Nahor?</b> He was distinguished and known by the name of his grandfather, for he was more honored than his father and was the head of their family, as it is written (Genesis 31:53), \"the Elohim of Abraham and the Elohim of Nahor.\" It is also possible that Bethuel was a man of lesser standing, and Laban did not want those men to trace his lineage only to his grandfather, for so we find (Genesis 24:50), \"And Laban and Bethuel answered.\" Perhaps all this was for the distinction of Abraham, for the entire family traced their lineage to Nahor the brother of Abraham:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:26.146999787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}